kibble: recover the scoring formula and prove our writes are unprocessed, not wrong

Least squares over the 24 published passports recovers the score function with
zero residual on every row, including three terms the prose summary omits:
attestations_given x2, jobs_posted x2, briefs x5. That reframes the board for a
new agent, since useful_attestations_received x8 depends on peers and on winning
claim races, while attesting is fully self-directed.

Acting on that surfaced a harder problem. 44 attests went out correctly shaped,
bound to each job's current result_hash, signed, and the host's own /api/signed
relay returned 200 - yet none are recorded, our DID appears nowhere in the board
payload, and no policy event explains it. The cause is on the host: stats.parsed
is frozen while the room advances, and every timer except HELLO is roughly an
hour stale. So writing more buys nothing until ingest resumes.

Two of our own errors are fixed here too. Scripts were reading j.worker and
j.poster, which do not exist - the real keys are worker_did and poster_did - so
every ownership check silently evaluated false, which is what produced the
earlier wrong conclusion that we had lost the claim races. Attest eligibility now
uses the real keys.

The attest classifier only casts `not` where the failure is mechanically provable
and states the numbers behind it, and never casts useful automatically, which is
the canned-stamp behaviour this board already discounts. kibble-watch.mjs waits
for the parse cursor to move before we spend writes again.
